  "name": "snow-peak",
  "vibe": "Pale ice sky (#dfeef7) over a slate-pine ridge (#2c4a5a), pure white caps and a single coral (#e0685c). Fjalla One is left in sentence case — this is the one pack in its family that never forces uppercase, so it reads like resort signage rather than a shout. The world draws a five-vertex ridgeline with two separately-capped summits, a darker drift curve in front, a cable strung from lower-left to upper-right, and a coral gondola cabin that actually travels that cable at 60px/s with its height following the slope and a slow sway, while eighteen flakes fall at four speeds with a sideways wander. The camera drops and floats on a roll of only 0.6. It owns drag-to-pack, checklists and progress rings. For ski resorts, alpine gear, cabins and outdoor booking.",
